codex
The bounded trace found the mismatch: the live caller continuation contains the statement-list tail `Return(Name("n")) .Stmts ~> #endcall ~> .K`, while my standalone loop claim had the semantically equivalent but syntactically narrower continuation without those list markers. I’ve strengthened the circularity to the exact continuation produced by the function body; this changes no semantics or summary equations.
exec
/bin/bash -lc 'kprove spec.k --definition verification-kompiled --spec-module SPEC --claims SPEC.loop' in /workspace
